; =====================================================================
; figure-6-3-formatted-string.derived.abnf
;
; DERIVED - not verbatim. Figure 6-3 of NISTIR 7695 (CPE Naming
; Specification Version 2.3, August 2011), "ABNF for Formatted String
; Binding", section 6.2.1, printed page 32, repaired so that it is
; valid RFC 5234 ABNF. The verbatim figure is
; figure-6-3-formatted-string.abnf beside this file.
;
; Root rule: formstring.
;
; Source PDF SHA-256
; 01553a4638b21eda10018690b71162e91605d78eb15850f881bd0b2b691ac3f6
;
; Role. Section 4, item 2: an implementation that produces CPE names
; "MUST produce syntactically correct formatted string bindings";
; item 4(a): one that consumes them "MUST consume syntactically correct
; formatted string bindings". 6.2: "Note that all eleven (11)
; attribute values MUST appear in the formatted string binding."
;
; The one repair, and nothing else (every other token is the figure's):
;   R1  The rule names sw_edition, target_sw, target_hw and spec_chrs
;       are written sw-edition, target-sw, target-hw and spec-chrs
;       (rule names allow letters, digits and hyphens only, RFC 2234
;       and RFC 5234 section 2.1).
;
; Readings kept from the figure, not repaired:
;   - RFC 2234 quoted strings are case-insensitive, so "CPE:2.3:" and
;     the part letters "A", "H", "O" match. The XML schema the
;     specification calls authoritative does not accept them;
;     run-fixtures.derived.py reports both readings.
;   - avstring needs at least one character that is not special, so a
;     lone "?" (allowed in a WFN by 5.3.2 item 4) cannot be written;
;     "-" alone matches both a one-character avstring and logical, and
;     6.2 settles it: used alone, the hyphen represents the logical
;     value NA.
;   - LANGTAG admits language ["-" region] only, a subset of RFC 5646
;     tags, though 5.3.3.10 says "any valid language tag MAY be used".
; =====================================================================

formstring           = "cpe:2.3:" component-list

component-list       = part ":" vendor ":" product ":" version ":" update ":"
                       edition ":" lang ":" sw-edition ":" target-sw ":"
                       target-hw ":" other

part                 = "h" / "o" / "a" / logical
vendor               = avstring
product              = avstring
version              = avstring
update               = avstring
edition              = avstring
lang                 = LANGTAG / logical
sw-edition           = avstring
target-sw            = avstring
target-hw            = avstring
other                = avstring
avstring             = *1spec-chrs 1*( unreserved / quoted ) *1spec-chrs / logical
spec-chrs            = 1*spec1 / spec2
logical              = "*" / "-"
special              = spec1 / spec2
spec1                = "?"
spec2                = "*"
unreserved           = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "." / "_"
quoted               = escape (escape / special / punc)
escape               = "\"
punc                 = "!" / DQUOTE / "#" / "$" / "%" / "&" / "'" / "(" / ")" /
                       "+" / "," / "/" / ":" / ";" / "<" / "=" / ">" / "@" /
                       "[" / "]" / "^" / "`" / "{" / "|" / "}" / "~"
ALPHA                = %x41-5a / %x61-7A   ; a-z
DIGIT                = %x30-39 ; 0-9
DQUOTE               = %x22 ; double-quote
LANGTAG              = language ["-" region] ; cf. [RFC5646]
language             = 2*3ALPHA              ; shortest ISO 639 code
region               = 2ALPHA / 3DIGIT       ; ISO 3166-1 code or UN M.49 code
